Subject: [PATCH 34/34] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20the=20program's=20menu,=20ke?=
 =?UTF-8?q?pt=20per=20screen,=20and=20its=20palette=20(SPEC=20=C2=A710.7)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The terminal tells hotty-blitz the screen it is on, when the host is
created and at each switch (hotty_host_set_screen, in place of
hide_menu): the alternate screen's menu goes when it is left, and the
level shown hides and the palette closes. The palette is a surface of
the host's own: the `palette` effect places it at the top centre,
above the menu, and the existing remove effect takes it away.

A new binding action, toggle_hotty_palette (ctrl+shift+space, cmd+shift
+space on macOS), opens and closes it. While it is open every key press
goes to hotty_host_palette_key and nothing else hears it, except the
toggle's own binding. A pick is sent as the Edit menu sends a command:
copy copies the selection, paste reads the clipboard first, the rest go
as commands with no key.

Upstream files: 20 lines (Binding.zig 10, Config.zig 7, Surface.zig 2,
command.zig 1); the rest is in src/termio/hotty.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
